BND-08: let a pondable node pond only above its surcharge depth

As in 5.3.0, a node with a ponded area ponded from its full depth up and its
surcharge depth was ignored, contrary to the input manual (Apond applies
"once water depth exceeds Ymax + Ysur"). Use full depth + surcharge depth as
the ponding threshold in DWSolver::setNodeDepth(), commitNodeDepthState(),
initNodeStates() and node::getPondedArea(), as the 5.3.0 patch does. A
2D-coupled junction keeps its rim threshold: its ponded area is its 2D cell.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-08_swmm600.patch

